<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Catalog>

    <!-- =====================================================================
         TARDIGRADE: LARVA FALLBACK BUILD BUTTONS
         The morph units Ravager / Lurker / Brood Lord / Baneling are given a
         direct larva-build path in AbilData.xml (LarvaTrain Train6/9/14/16) so
         they stay buildable even if their morph parent was banned. Those train
         options need command-card buttons on the Larva.

         Each button is placed on its PARENT's cell (Roach / Hydralisk /
         Corruptor / Zergling). This works because a fallback button only
         appears when its parent unit is disabled (undrafted) - and when the
         parent is gone, that cell is free. If both parent and child are
         drafted (rare, since the child builds directly) the two overlap.

         NOTE: the Larva card is dense and merged across several data layers -
         VERIFY these slots in the editor's Command Card view and nudge any
         that overlap an always-present button.
    ===================================================================== -->
    <CUnit id="Larva">
        <CardLayouts index="0">
            <LayoutButtons Face="Ravager"   Type="AbilCmd" AbilCmd="LarvaTrain,Train6"  Row="1" Column="0"/>
            <LayoutButtons Face="LurkerMP"  Type="AbilCmd" AbilCmd="LarvaTrain,Train9"  Row="1" Column="1"/>
            <LayoutButtons Face="BroodLord" Type="AbilCmd" AbilCmd="LarvaTrain,Train14" Row="2" Column="1"/>
            <LayoutButtons Face="Baneling"  Type="AbilCmd" AbilCmd="LarvaTrain,Train16" Row="0" Column="2"/>
        </CardLayouts>
    </CUnit>

    <!-- =====================================================================
         TARDIGRADE: MODIFIER ABILITY GRANTS
         Battle Blink and Medivac Boost (see AbilData.xml) are granted, hidden,
         to every combat unit and worker across all three races so the ability
         exists to show/hide at runtime. CycleMod.galaxy toggles visibility
         per-unit based on which side drafted which modifier - a unit whose
         side didn't draft either keeps both hidden all game.

         A granted ability with no CardLayouts entry has nowhere to render -
         UnitAbilityShow toggling it "visible" does nothing if the command
         card never reserved it a cell (confirmed against Blizzard's own
         pattern: their KD8Charge patch to the Reaper ships an AbilArray grant
         paired with an explicit CardLayouts slot, not a bare grant). Every
         unit below therefore gets an explicit slot: Blink at Row 1 Column 2,
         Medivac Boost at Row 1 Column 3 - deliberately different columns of
         the SAME row so both can be shown and used at once, not one hiding
         behind the other.

         History: Row 3 (tried first, on the theory that no vanilla unit's
         LayoutButtons ever used it) turned out not to render at all in the
         live editor - the command-card panel apparently caps at 3 visible
         rows regardless of what the data allows. Row 1 Column 0/1 (tried
         next) DID render, but playtesting across several units found it
         collides with existing vanilla buttons often enough to matter
         (e.g. Ghost's Nuke/WeaponsFree, Infestor's Fungal Growth tend to
         sit in the low columns). Column 2/3 - still Row 1, just further
         right - was chosen as less occupied based on that same testing.
         Still not individually verified for all 52 units below; if a button
         is missing or covers up a different ability on a specific one, nudge
         its Row/Column in that unit's CardLayouts entry.
    ===================================================================== -->
